From d89d70de5771425f7fd7bbae0600cb6f2e957352 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:42:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tenant): add model-level cross-organization FK integrity
 guard

Phase 1.5 doc 01 rule 4 and doc 05's Relationships test matrix require that
foreign-key relationships never permit cross-organization references.
Isolation was previously enforced only at the serializer layer
(TenantScopedModelSerializer / TenantScopedPrimaryKeyRelatedField) - nothing
stopped a cross-tenant FK from Django admin, a management command, a data
migration, or a future call site that builds a model instance directly.

- core/models.py: BaseModel.assert_same_organization() - skips related
  objects that are None or whose organization isn't set yet (legacy
  nullable rows from the staged Phase 1 backfill); raises ValidationError
  on a genuine mismatch.
- Wired into save() for MonographTest, Product, Batch, SamplePull,
  LocationHistory, TestPoint, TestResult, ResultReview, ResultCorrection.
- apps/chamber/serializers.py: LocationHistorySerializer.batch marked
  read-only (currently only used for read, but was a bare unscoped
  PrimaryKeyRelatedField waiting for a future create endpoint to trip over).
- apps/products/tests/factories.py, apps/batches/tests/factories.py: fixed
  two pre-existing factory bugs the new guard surfaced immediately -
  MonographTestFactory/ProductFactory/BatchFactory derived organization
  independently of their monograph/product SubFactory defaults, so calling
  e.g. ProductFactory(organization=org_b) silently produced a Product in
  org B pointing at a Monograph in some unrelated auto-created org. Fixed
  by propagating the resolved organization into the nested SubFactory via
  SelfAttribute.
- core/tests/test_cross_organization_fk_integrity.py: new regression suite,
  one test per relationship in doc 05's Relationships matrix.

Full suite: 227 passed, 0 failed.
